  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_pov: Geralt-centered third person"
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_participants: Geralt; Zephyr; Oreck; Sythara; twelve juveniles including Vorrik and Kree; Five Mikas (elemental/remote effects)"
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_focus: Geralt enters Oreck's settlement, encounters Sythara and the twelve-child household, reunites with Oreck, explains Karvex and the Ledger, recruits Oreck, witnesses the family farewells, and departs with him."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_boundary_evidence: Arrival at a separately staged destination after three weeks of travel."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "The settlement entry, family encounter, reunion, Ledger discussion, recruitment, farewell, and walk away are one continuous visit without a time or POV reset."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_oreck_state: Legitimate continuation of his unresolved Settlement-Year-5 departure, not resurrection."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "Alive, armorless, cleaver-equipped, chroniton augmentations functioning, living in an eastern mesa/canyon settlement with mate Sythara and a twelve-child household."
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_oreck_hidden_history: Unshown when he reached the settlement, when he met Sythara, how the settlement formed, what his original eastward objective was, and whether each child is biological, adopted, or part of a pre-existing family."
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_child-age_continuity: Family history unresolved; oldest child's age predates Oreck's shown settlement interval and therefore cannot be assumed to represent a child conceived after his Falcon Ridge departure."
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "Sythara's pre-existing children, adoption, and non-human reproductive history remain possible but unestablished."
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_mika_contamination: Chapter 049 strongly appears to conflate active-continuity Mika with an Oreck-wife draft history and relocates her grave toward the eastern canyon."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "A separate second Mika is theoretically possible but is not established by the manuscript."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "Active continuity retains Mika as Geralt's dead wife/partner buried at Falcon Ridge; this is not resurrection."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_zephyr_state: Present and recognized by Oreck, but still provides no shown preparation, training, instruction, transformation, or armor evolution."
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_geralt_state: Physically unaged; no new bodily capability or Faraxar-memory restoration."
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_dragon_mail_state: Responsive dormant second skin; Stage 1 remains highest established; old cracked plates and bent left wing remain unrepaired on-page."
  - line: 28
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_flight_capability: No wing deployment or sustained flight."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_zaron_state: Entirely absent; armor reactions are not attributed to Zaron."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_applicator_state: Active head-Applicator produces targeting reticules, analyzes Sythara, juveniles, Oreck, emotions, and Oreck's cleaver, and communicates in First Tongue with Violet's harmonic beneath its code."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Its identity, persistence, and prior silence remain unexplained."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_luminaire_echo_/_companion_state: No coherent Luminaire or named Companion Protocol yet; generic network sensing remains distinct from the Applicator."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_luminara_vessel_state: Chapter 041 material vessel unresolved."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_protocol_key_state: Unmentioned and unused."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_sound_fragment_state: Forest and Plains fragments undelivered; third/Fourth Fragment unresolved."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_five_state: Remote elemental actors enforce calm and are described as always with Geralt."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Their chamber, original-body, awakening, Affinity Core, training, and transformation history remains unshown."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_five_/_count_state: \"For the 250."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "For the Five\" grammatically distinguishes the groups, but 249 versus 250 and Chapter 048's contaminated Five history remain unresolved."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_faraxar_memory_state: Still altered or inaccessible."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_karvex_/_ledger_state: Karvex is reported but does not return; contract remains suspended, and Oreck commits to finding and erasing the Ledger."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_node_gamma_state: Absent; twelve-shard outcome unresolved."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_sath'rak_state: Warning remains abandoned/unresolved."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_time-travel_state: No global model established."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_hidden_interval: Oreck's route, settlement founding, family formation, and all household history before Geralt's arrival are unstaged."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_contradictions: Mika-wife/grave contamination; unexplained family history; unexplained Applicator reappearance; unresolved 249/250 history."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_chronological_overlap: References to Mika, Karvex, the Five, and the 250 are retrospective rather than duplicate events."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_presentation: settlement arrival / family reunion / recruitment / farewell cutscene"
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_cutscene_purpose: Recover Oreck from his unresolved departure, reveal the life he built, and recruit him into the Ledger mission."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "@contract: engain.scene_text_packet.v1"
  - line: 51
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 52
