  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "```"
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck’s settlement was a clutch of dwellings wedged into a mesa."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "Defensible."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "Isolated."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "A perfect place for a predator to hide, or a father to guard his nest."
  - line: 110
    type: narration
    text: "The dragon armor, a dormant second skin, constricted minutely around Geralt’s ribs as he approached the main door."
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "A threat assessment he didn’t need."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "The door opened."
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian woman (Sythara) was a tactical equation."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator solved it instantly:"
  - line: 117
    type: narration
    text: "Subject: Female Reptilian."
  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "Height: 2.03m."
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "Muscle density: High."
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "Scar clusters (old combat): Right flank, left forearm."
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "Stance: Defensive/Guarding."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "Probable mate-bond to primary target (Oreck)."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "Threat Level: Moderate-High."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "Suggestion: Disarm first."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt ignored it. “I’m Geralt.”"
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "“I know."
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "He dreams loud.” Her slitted amber eyes didn’t blink. “You bring the end of things with you."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "I can smell it on the wind.”"
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "“I’m here to talk.”"
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "“Talk is the prelude,” she said, but stepped aside."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "The armor on Geralt’s shoulders loosened a fraction."
  - line: 134
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 2: THE FAMILY - A CALCULATION OF VULNERABILITIES"
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "Inside: chaos, warmth, life."
  - line: 139
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator went haywire, painting his vision with targeting reticules."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "Multiple juvenile bio-signs: 12."
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "Age range: 0.8 - 10.3 Earth-standard years."
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "Aggregation pattern: Curious/Threatened."
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "Threat Level: Negligible."
  - line: 144
    type: narration
    text: "Note: High-pitched vocalizations may trigger stress response."
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "They were everywhere."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "Clinging to shelves, peering from behind woven hangings."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "One dropped from the ceiling, landing with a soft thump."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt’s hand twitched, the armor plating on his forearm snapping an inch from his skin before he forced it down."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "The oldest juvenile (Vorrik) stepped forward, a stick in his hand."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator tagged him: Juvenile Male."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "Developing combat posture."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Adrenaline elevated."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "“You’re the Storm-that-Walks."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "The Breaker.”"
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "“I was,” Geralt said, his voice too rough for this room full of soft sounds."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "“Did you come to break us?”"
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "Before he could answer, a small weight hit his leg."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "He looked down."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "A hatchling."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "Designation: Kree."
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "She had climbed him and now stared up, her large, dark eyes holding no fear, only profound, stupid curiosity."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "Her tiny claws pricked through his trousers."
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "Her tail was a vise around his calf."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "Bio-signature: Elevated heart rate, curiosity/excitement pheromones detected."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "Threat: None."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Suggested action: Remove."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn’t move."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "He was frozen by the sheer, terrifying fragility of it."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "Sythara sighed. “Kree."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "He is not a tree.”"
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "Kree chirped, a sound like grinding stones, and nuzzled her head against his knee."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "Vorrik smirked. “She imprints on the biggest source of heat."
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "You’re stuck."
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "Father says it’s a death-grip.”"
  - line: 181
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 3: ORECK EMERGES - THE UNCHANGED VARIABLE"
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "The back door opened."
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck filled it."
  - line: 188
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator flashed a crimson summary:"
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "Subject: Oreck."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "Status: Prime physical condition."
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "Chroniton decay signature: Stable."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "Weapon (Cleaver): Not in hand."
  - line: 193
    type: narration
    text: "Psychological profile: Elevated protective instinct."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "Threat Level: Extreme."
  - line: 196
    type: narration
    text: "He had changed."
  - line: 197
    type: narration
    text: "The fury was banked, buried under a layer of domestic calm."
  - line: 198
    type: narration
    text: "But Geralt saw it in the way his eyes scanned the room in a millisecond—checking exits, threats, children—before landing on him."
  - line: 200
    type: narration
    text: "The silence was a physical pressure."
  - line: 201
    type: narration
    text: "The hearth fire guttered and turned a sudden, profound blue for three full seconds."
  - line: 202
    type: narration
    text: "Red, reacting to the surge of old, bonded power in the room."
  - line: 204
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck crossed the space."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t grip Geralt’s shoulder."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "He stopped a foot away, his nostrils flaring as he sampled Geralt’s scent—stress, travel, ozone, and the faint, iron smell of the dragon armor."
  - line: 207
    type: narration
    text: "“You stink of void and old blood,” Oreck rumbled."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "“You smell of clay and milk,” Geralt replied."
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck’s gaze flicked down to Kree."
  - line: 211
    type: narration
    text: "A change came over him."
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "The warrior’s mask dissolved."
  - line: 213
    type: narration
    text: "He crouched, his massive hand enveloping the hatchling. “Little ember."
  - line: 214
    type: narration
    text: "You burn too bright.” His touch was impossibly gentle."
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "Kree chirped and transferred her grip to his wrist, scaling his arm to perch on his shoulder."
  - line: 217
    type: narration
    text: "“This is Sythara."
  - line: 218
    type: narration
    text: "My heart.” He gestured. “These are my reasons for breathing.” He looked at Geralt, and the mask was back, but cracked. “You met Mika."
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "My late wife.”"
  - line: 220
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt nodded. “I stood at her stone.”"
  - line: 221
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck’s jaw tightened."
  - line: 222
    type: narration
    text: "A minute flare of chroniton energy sparked in his eyes. “She wanted this."
  - line: 223
    type: narration
    text: "The quiet."
  - line: 224
    type: narration
    text: "The clan.” He looked at the children. “She didn’t live to see it.”"
  - line: 226
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 228
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 4: THE CONVERSATION - THE MORAL ALGORITHM"
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "They sat."
  - line: 231
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck didn’t take his eyes off Geralt. “Zephyr’s presence means this is history moving."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "So."
  - line: 233
    type: narration
    text: "Speak.”"
  - line: 235
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt told him."
  - line: 236
    type: narration
    text: "Karvex."
  - line: 237
    type: narration
    text: "The Ledger-Born."
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "The debt of “unfinished stories.” The Five Mikas."
  - line: 239
    type: narration
    text: "Their new name."
  - line: 240
    type: narration
    text: "Their intervention."
  - line: 242
    type: narration
    text: "As he spoke, the applicator fed him data on Oreck:"
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "Heart rate: Increasing."
  - line: 244
    type: narration
    text: "Pupil dilation: 18%."
  - line: 245
    type: narration
    text: "Galvanic skin response: Spiking."
  - line: 246
    type: narration
    text: "Conclusion: Subject experiencing high stress/anger."
  - line: 248
    type: narration
    text: "When Geralt finished, Oreck was silent for a full minute."
  - line: 249
    type: narration
    text: "Then he laughed, a short, bitter sound. “A debt."
  - line: 250
    type: narration
    text: "For stories.” He leaned forward, and his voice dropped to a sub-audible growl the children couldn’t hear. “I buried my story with my wife on a hill overlooking this canyon, Geralt."
  - line: 251
    type: narration
    text: "I poured it into the foundations of this home."
  - line: 252
    type: narration
    text: "I let my children chew on its bones."
  - line: 253
    type: narration
    text: "It is done.”"
  - line: 255
    type: narration
    text: "“The ledger says it’s not.”"
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "“FUCK THE LEDGER!” Oreck roared, surging to his feet."
  - line: 258
    type: narration
    text: "The reaction was instantaneous."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "The hearth fire exploded upwards in a silent pillar of blue-white flame (Red, shielding the children from heat)."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "The stone floor rippled like water (Green, steadying the structures)."
  - line: 261
    type: narration
    text: "The air pressure spiked (White, muffling the sound)."
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "The water in a clay jug froze, then boiled (Blue, a display of controlled power)."
  - line: 264
    type: narration
    text: "The Five Mikas had just enforced calm."
  - line: 266
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck stood panting, feeling the elemental lockdown."
  - line: 267
    type: narration
    text: "He looked from the silent, powerful displays to Geralt, and understanding dawned—horrible and cold. “They are always with you.”"
  - line: 268
    type: narration
    text: "“Yes.”"
  - line: 269
    type: narration
    text: "“And they say this debt is real.”"
  - line: 270
    type: narration
    text: "“They interceded."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "The debt is real enough for cosmic bailiffs."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "It’s suspended, not gone.”"
  - line: 274
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck sank back down."
  - line: 275
    type: narration
    text: "All the fight left him."
  - line: 276
    type: narration
    text: "He looked at Sythara, and his voice broke. “If I stay… they will send another."
  - line: 277
    type: narration
    text: "And another."
  - line: 278
    type: narration
    text: "They will come here."
  - line: 279
    type: narration
    text: "To our home.”"
  - line: 280
    type: narration
    text: "Sythara’s face was stone, but a single, clear tear tracked down her scaled cheek."
  - line: 281
    type: narration
    text: "She knew. “You must make them stop."
  - line: 282
    type: narration
    text: "Permanently.”"
  - line: 283
    type: narration
    text: "“I can’t protect you if I’m here,” he whispered, the words a confession of utter failure."
  - line: 284
    type: narration
    text: "“You can’t protect us if you are dead in a canyon far away, either,” she said, her voice iron. “So you will go."
  - line: 285
    type: narration
    text: "You will settle this."
  - line: 286
    type: narration
    text: "And you will return."
  - line: 287
    type: narration
    text: "That is the only acceptable algorithm.”"
  - line: 289
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 291
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 5: THE DECISION - A CONTRACT IN BLOOD AND DATA"
  - line: 293
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck stood."
  - line: 294
    type: narration
    text: "He went to the wall, took down the cleaver."
  - line: 295
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator in Geralt’s head chimed."
  - line: 296
    type: narration
    text: "Weapon Analysis: Monomolecular edge."
  - line: 297
    type: narration
    text: "Chroniton-forged core."
  - line: 298
    type: narration
    text: "Blood residue (old) matches Subject: Oreck, Subject: Geralt, 43 unknown entities."
  - line: 299
    type: narration
    text: "Lethality rating: Maximum."
  - line: 301
    type: narration
    text: "He held it, then turned to Geralt. “The debt."
  - line: 302
    type: narration
    text: "Is it mine?"
  - line: 303
    type: narration
    text: "Or is it ours?”"
  - line: 304
    type: narration
    text: "“The Ledger-Born named me."
  - line: 305
    type: narration
    text: "But the debt is for ‘unfinished stories.’ Our story is unfinished, brother.”"
  - line: 306
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck nodded."
  - line: 307
    type: narration
    text: "He walked to the hearth, reached in, and pulled a glowing ember out with his bare hand."
  - line: 308
    type: narration
    text: "He knelt before Sythara and pressed the ember to the scales over his heart."
  - line: 309
    type: narration
    text: "It sizzled."
  - line: 310
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t flinch."
  - line: 311
    type: narration
    text: "“My life-fire is here."
  - line: 312
    type: narration
    text: "With you."
  - line: 313
    type: narration
    text: "With them."
  - line: 314
    type: narration
    text: "I go as a shell to burn out the past.” He looked at Geralt, his eyes reflecting the dying ember. “I will come."
  - line: 315
    type: narration
    text: "On one condition."
  - line: 316
    type: narration
    text: "We do not just fight the next collector."
  - line: 317
    type: narration
    text: "We find the Ledger itself."
  - line: 318
    type: narration
    text: "We don’t settle the debt."
  - line: 319
    type: narration
    text: "We erase it."
  - line: 320
    type: narration
    text: "For us."
  - line: 321
    type: narration
    text: "For the 250."
  - line: 322
    type: narration
    text: "For the Five."
  - line: 323
    type: narration
    text: "For every story they called ‘unfinished.’ We burn the bank.”"
  - line: 325
    type: narration
    text: "The dragon armor across Geralt’s chest flared hot, then cooled, the plates aligning with a new, fierce purpose."
  - line: 326
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator displayed a single, scrolling line of text, not in its usual dialect, but in the jagged script of the First Tongue: < Path Calculated: Foundation Through Fire."
  - line: 327
    type: narration
    text: "Probability of Success: 0.00%."
  - line: 328
    type: narration
    text: "Proceed? >"
  - line: 330
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt smiled, a thin, dangerous smile. “Yes.”"
  - line: 332
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 334
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 6: THE FAREWELL - DATA LOSS"
  - line: 336
    type: narration
    text: "The goodbye was a quiet, systematic dismantling of a life."
  - line: 338
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck did not kneel to the children."
  - line: 339
    type: narration
    text: "He stood, a monument, and gave them orders."
  - line: 340
    type: narration
    text: "“Vorrik."
  - line: 341
    type: narration
    text: "You are the warm stone now."
  - line: 342
    type: narration
    text: "You do not move.”"
  - line: 343
    type: narration
    text: "“Yes, Father.”"
  - line: 344
    type: narration
    text: "“Kessa, Varn."
  - line: 345
    type: narration
    text: "You are the eyes on the high rock.”"
  - line: 346
    type: narration
    text: "“Yes, Father.”"
  - line: 347
    type: narration
    text: "One by one, he assigned them roles, duties, a purpose in the ecosystem of the family to hold it together in his absence."
  - line: 349
    type: narration
    text: "Then he came to Kree, still on his shoulder."
  - line: 350
    type: narration
    text: "He took her, held her before his face. “You, little ember."
  - line: 351
    type: narration
    text: "You are the spark."
  - line: 352
    type: narration
    text: "You keep the home-fire burning."
  - line: 353
    type: narration
    text: "You remind them of joy."
  - line: 354
    type: narration
    text: "Can you do that?”"
  - line: 355
    type: narration
    text: "She chirped, a sad, confused sound."
  - line: 356
    type: narration
    text: "He pressed his forehead to hers."
  - line: 357
    type: narration
    text: "Then he placed her in Sythara’s arms."
  - line: 359
    type: narration
    text: "He did not look back."
  - line: 360
    type: narration
    text: "He couldn’t."
  - line: 361
    type: narration
    text: "The applicator in Geralt’s head, scanning him, gave a final, bleak readout:"
  - line: 362
    type: narration
    text: "Subject: Oreck."
  - line: 363
    type: narration
    text: "Vital signs: Within parameters."
  - line: 364
    type: narration
    text: "Psychological state: Catastrophic grief."
  - line: 365
    type: narration
    text: "Note: Subject is operating in tactical mode only."
  - line: 366
    type: narration
    text: "Emotional processors offline."
  - line: 368
    type: narration
    text: "They walked out of the canyon."
  - line: 369
    type: narration
    text: "The sound that followed them was not crying."
  - line: 370
    type: narration
    text: "It was Sythara singing a low, grinding dirge in the reptilian tongue—a song for the walking dead."
  - line: 372
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 374
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 7: THE ROAD AHEAD - A NEW QUERY"
  - line: 376
    type: narration
    text: "They walked until the settlement was a speck."
  - line: 378
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck spoke, his voice a dry rasp. “The armor you wear."
  - line: 379
    type: narration
    text: "The thing in your head."
  - line: 380
    type: narration
    text: "Do they tell you how to feel?”"
  - line: 381
    type: narration
    text: "“No,” Geralt said. “They just tell me what is.”"
  - line: 382
    type: narration
    text: "“What am I?”"
  - line: 383
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt looked at the readout."
  - line: 384
    type: narration
    text: "Subject: Oreck."
  - line: 385
    type: narration
    text: "Threat Level: Extreme."
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "Ally Integrity: 100%."
  - line: 387
    type: narration
    text: "“You are my brother."
  - line: 388
    type: narration
    text: "And we are going to burn the bank.”"
  - line: 390
    type: narration
    text: "Ahead, the badlands shimmered."
  - line: 391
    type: narration
    text: "The network felt thin, but the Five Mikas were a steady hum in the elements."
  - line: 392
    type: narration
    text: "The wind carried a new query, whispered from the applicator in a voice that was both digital and deeply familiar—Violet’s harmonic layered beneath the code."
  - line: 394
    type: narration
    text: "< Query: What is a king without a crown?>"
  - line: 395
    type: narration
    text: "< Query: What is a storm without a sky?>"
  - line: 396
    type: narration
    text: "< Query: What is a debt if there is no ledger?>"
  - line: 398
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt had no answer."
  - line: 399
    type: narration
    text: "Not yet."
  - line: 401
    type: narration
    text: "But for the first time, the silence felt like a question worth answering."
  - line: 403
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"

